{"name":"Bluebonnet","hex":"#1c1cf0","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bluebonnet","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of blue bonnet."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bluebonnet"}],"entries":[{"title":"The Blue Bonnet","blocks":[{"text":"The Blue Bonnet is a 1919 American silent drama film directed by Louis Chaudet and starring Billie Rhodes, Ben F. Wilson, and Irene Rich."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/The_Blue_Bonnet_%281919%29_-_Ad_1.jpg/330px-The_Blue_Bonnet_%281919%29_-_Ad_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Blue_Bonnet"},{"title":"Blue Bonnet (brand)","blocks":[{"text":"Blue Bonnet is an American brand of margarine and other bread spreads and baking fats, owned by ConAgra Foods. Original owner Standard Brands merged with Nabisco in July 1981, but Nabisco ultimately sold Blue Bonnet to ConAgra, along with a number of other food brands, in 1998."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue_Bonnet_(brand)"},{"title":"Bluebonnet (plant)","blocks":[{"text":"Bluebonnet is a name given to any of a number of purple-flowered or blue-flowered species of the genus Lupinus and is collectively the state flower of Texas. The shape of the petals on the flower resembles the bonnet worn by pioneer women to shield them from the sun.\nSpecies often called bluebonnets include:"},{"items":["Lupinus argenteus, silvery lupine","Lupinus concinnus, Bajada lupine","Lupinus havardii, Big Bend bluebonnet or Chisos bluebonnet","Lupinus perennis, wild lupine or blue lupine","Lupinus plattensis, Nebraska lupine","Lupinus subcarnosus, sandyland bluebonnet or buffalo clover","Lupinus texensis, Texas bluebonnet or Texas lupine"]}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Bluebonnet-8100.jpg/330px-Bluebonnet-8100.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bluebonnet_(plant)"},{"title":"Bluebonnet (bird)","blocks":[{"text":"Bluebonnets, as they are commonly referred to, are small species of parrots native to Australia and classed within the Northiella genus—the eastern bluebonnet and the Naretha bluebonnet. The genus is named in honour of Australian ornithologist Alfred John North."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Northiella_haematogaster_-Cocoparra_National_Park-8.jpg/330px-Northiella_haematogaster_-Cocoparra_National_Park-8.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bluebonnet_(bird)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Blue_Bonnet_ad_from_The_Ladies%27_home_journal_%281948%29_%2814763987001%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Blue_Bonnet_ad_from_The_Ladies%27_home_journal_%281948%29_%2814763987001%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Blue_Bonnet_ad_from_The_Ladies%27_home_journal_%281948%29_%2814763987001%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/1280px-Blue_Bonnet_ad_from_The_Ladies%27_home_journal_%281948%29_%2814763987001%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Blue_Bonnet_ad_from_The_Ladies%27_home_journal_%281948%29_%2814763987001%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Blue_Bonnet_ad_from_The_Ladies%27_home_journal_%281948%29_%2814763987001%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"1948 advertisement in Ladies' Home Journal","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABlue_Bonnet_ad_from_The_Ladies'_home_journal_(1948)_(14763987001)_(cropped).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Texas_Blue-Bonnet_--_Lupinus.jpg/500px-Texas_Blue-Bonnet_--_Lupinus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Texas_Blue-Bonnet_--_Lupinus.jpg/1280px-Texas_Blue-Bonnet_--_Lupinus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Texas_Blue-Bonnet_--_Lupinus.jpg/500px-Texas_Blue-Bonnet_--_Lupinus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Texas bluebonnet -- Lupinus","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATexas_Blue-Bonnet_--_Lupinus.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Distributionofbluebonnet.png/330px-Distributionofbluebonnet.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Distributionofbluebonnet.png/330px-Distributionofbluebonnet.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Distribution of the Northiella genus.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADistributionofbluebonnet.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Bluebonnet-back.jpg/500px-Bluebonnet-back.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Bluebonnet-back.jpg/1280px-Bluebonnet-back.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Bluebonnet-back.jpg/500px-Bluebonnet-back.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABluebonnet-back.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Naretha_Bluebonnet_hen.jpg/500px-Naretha_Bluebonnet_hen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/